1. WHAT THIS COVERS

   This licence covers the original work in this repository: the application
   source code, the recipe text and method steps, the nutrition and food
   composition tables, the design, the copy in all six languages, and the
   mascot artwork as arranged, cut and posed for this app.

   It does NOT cover the third-party material this app uses. That material is
   listed in CREDITS.md and stays under its own terms — OpenStreetMap and
   Open Food Facts data under the Open Database Licence, the dish photographs
   under their individual Creative Commons licences, and the Caprasimo and
   Figtree typefaces under the SIL Open Font License. Those terms are
   obligations, not preferences: the attribution rendered on the Settings,
   Locate and Shop screens is part of how this app is allowed to exist, and
   removing it breaks the licence rather than tidying the interface.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Use the app at pantryglobe.com, or any copy of it supplied to you, for
   cooking. Cook the recipes. Print one for your kitchen wall. Feed people,
   including people who pay you for dinner.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Without prior written permission you may not copy, modify, merge, publish,
   distribute, sublicense, sell, host, or create derivative works from this
   software or its content; you may not republish the recipe collection, the
   composition tables or the translations as your own, in whole or in
   substantial part; and you may not reverse-engineer, decompile or
   disassemble any compiled form of it.

   The app is delivered to your browser as readable JavaScript, because that
   is how the web works. Being able to read it is not permission to take it.

4. TRADE MARKS

   "Pantry", the Pantry wordmark, the pantryglobe.com identity, and the
   character — the cream canister with the brown lid, the brass plate and the
   wooden spoon — are trade marks of the Pantry authors, whether or not
   registered. Nothing in this licence grants any right to use them. In
   particular, a permitted use of the code under section 2 is not permission
   to use the name or the character.

5. NO WARRANTY

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL
   THE AUTHORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN
   AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN
   CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

   Prices are estimates, allergen filters read ingredient lists rather than
   packets, and cooking times are a guide. The Terms screen in the app says
   this in the language the reader chose, which is where it matters.

6. ASKING

   Permission for anything section 3 withholds is available by asking. The
   address is privacy@pantryglobe.com and a licensing request will reach a
